<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Krishna River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> is one of the major rivers of peninsular <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, flowing about 1,300 kilometres from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-ghats">Western Ghats</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a> east across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telangana">Telangana</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-pradesh">Andhra Pradesh</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-bengal">Bay of Bengal</a>. Its fertile lower valley and delta supported the Satavahanas, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ikshvaku">Ikshvakus</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagarjunakonda">Nagarjunakonda</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-chalukyas">Eastern Chalukyas</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vengi">Vengi</a>, and it often marked the frontier between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> powers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/krishna-river.jpg" alt="Krishna River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Munna Aawara · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Back_Water_View.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
